+<!--Copyright (C) 1988-2022 by George Mason University. See file COPYRIGHT for more information.-->
+
+<html>
+<head>
+<title>GrADS Function: percentile</title>
+</head>
+<body bgcolor="e0f0ff" text="#000000">
+
+<h2><b>percentile()</b></h2>
+<p>
+<code>percentile(<i>expr, dim1, dim2, pct <,tinc></i>)</code>
+
+<p>
+Returns a percentile of <code><i>expr</i></code> over the specified
+dimension range. Missing and non-finite values are omitted. If the reduction dimension
+is time, an optional time increment <code><i>tinc</i></code> may be
+specified.
+
+<p>
+<ul>
+<code><i>expr</i>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</code>- any valid GrADS expression<br>
+<code><i>dim1</i>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</code>- the start point of the reduction<br>
+<code><i>dim2</i>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</code>- the end point of the reduction<br>
+<code><i>pct</i>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</code>- percentile from 0 through 100<br>
+<code><i>tinc</i>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</code>- optional increment for a time reduction<br>
+</ul>
+
+<p>
+<code><i>dim1</i></code> and <code><i>dim2</i></code> are standard
+GrADS dimension expressions and must refer to the same dimension. X, Y,
+Z, T, and E reductions are supported. A gridded default file and a gridded
+expression are required; station data are not supported.
+
+<h3>Usage Notes</h3>
+<ol>
+<li>Values are equally weighted. Geographic grid spacing and latitude
+weights are not applied.</li>
+<li>The result uses linear interpolation between adjacent sorted values,
+with rank <code>(N-1)*pct/100</code> (Hyndman and Fan type 7).</li>
+<li>If one valid value is present it is returned for every percentile. If
+no valid values are present, the result is missing.</li>
+<li><code>percentile(...,0)</code> and
+<code>percentile(...,100)</code> are equivalent to the minimum and maximum
+values over the selected samples.</li>
+<li>Only grid points inside the requested range are sampled; endpoints
+are not spatially interpolated. The percentile value itself is interpolated
+between sorted samples as described above.</li>
+<li>The optional time increment is a positive integer number of grid steps
+or a duration such as <code>6hr</code>, <code>1dy</code>, or <code>1mo</code>.
+It must be an exact multiple of the file's time step. Calendar-month and
+fixed-length units may not be mixed.</li>
+<li>Memory usage is proportional to the number of samples multiplied by
+the number of output grid points (approximately 9 bytes per pair, plus
+sorting workspace). Reduce the domain or process smaller tiles if needed.</li>
+</ol>
+
+<h3>Examples</h3>
+<p>
+The ensemble median, and the lower and upper limits of a central
+90-percent ensemble interval, may be evaluated with:
+<p>
+<code>
+percentile(z,e=1,e=100,50)<br>
+percentile(z,e=1,e=100,5)<br>
+percentile(z,e=1,e=100,95)
+</code>
+
+<p>
+The 90th percentile over every fourth time step is:
+<p>
+<code>percentile(temp,t=1,t=120,90,4)</code>
+
+</body>
+</html>
